            "review_title": "Review at Café Blue Lagoon Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Roger N\nBedlington, United Kingdom634 contributions\n0\nStaying at resort ate here a couple of times\nFeb 2019 • Couples\nSignificantly more pricey than places outside, understandable given their overheads and staffing. Menu is in a glossy book so no changes at all day after day. As a vegetarian I found it very limited and really they need to up their game - if you don’t like Tofu you have almost nothing you can eat. Staff are nice and in the main understand the many languages they are faced with. I guess it benefits from the inherent unwillingness of guests to step outside the resort.\nRead more\nWritten February 28, 2019\nPandanusResort\nThank you again for choosing the Pandanus Resort for your first ever stay in a resort.\n\nAs for your comments regarding the Cafe Blue Lagoon Restaurant, of course the prices inside a luxury resort are going to be higher than those at the street-side restaurants outside of the resort. This would be true anywhere in the world. For one thing, the outside restaurants do not have the overhead that we do, nor do they offer the ambiance.\n\nAlthough our menu is a \"glossy book\", as you described it, there are 131 items on the menu, plus we offer daily specials. Therefore, it is not 'limited' by anyone's definition. Also, we have 10 items on our Vietnamese vegetarian page and 20 vegetarian items on our western portion of the menu. Only a few of them have tofu as an ingredient. Besides these 30 items from which to choose, many of the other items can be served without meat or fish if requested.\nRead more\nWritten June 15, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
